    "created_at": "2025-03-07T11:42:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-07T11:42:07Z",
    "body": "`\"auto\"` is not a valid keyword enumeration for `closedby`, but `Auto` is a valid state for it. States don't necessarily map to keywords. This means `closedby` has custom reflection rules for the `.closedBy`, and in fact it does: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#dom-dialog-closedby. It calls the `computed closed-by state`, which says if the attribute is in the `Auto` state it can return either the `Close Request` state (which will map to `\"closerequest\"`) or the `None` state (which will map to `\"none\"`).\n\nIn other words, the `Auto` state will reflect as two different enumerated keywords, either `\"closerequest\"` or `\"none\"`, depending on some logic elsewhere specified.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
